<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Lower Burgundy</h1><p class="st-meta">879 CE – 933 CE (approx.) · capital Vienne</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The kingdom of Provence founded by Boso in 879, the first realm in the Carolingian West to elect a king from outside the Carolingian family.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 879, after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-stammerer">Louis the Stammerer</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> and nobles meeting at Mantaille elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boso-of-provence">Boso</a>, a brother-in-law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a>, as king of the lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienne">Vienne</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-provence">Provence</a>. The Carolingian kings besieged Vienne in 880–882, but Boso's family kept control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> valley.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom was a loose union of counties along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> and in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-provence">Provence</a>, governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienne">Vienne</a> with strong support from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boso-of-provence">Boso</a>'s son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-blind">Louis the Blind</a> was crowned emperor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 901 but was captured and blinded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berengar-i-of-italy">Berengar of Italy</a> in 905. Afterwards real power lay with his kinsman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-of-arles">Hugh of Arles</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-of-arles">Hugh of Arles</a>, busy with his ambitions as king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, gave up his claims to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-ii-of-burgundy">Rudolf II of Upper Burgundy</a> around 933. The two Burgundian kingdoms were then united as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-arles">Kingdom of Arles</a>, which later passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-lower-burgundy.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Lower Burgundy" width="320" height="340"><figcaption>Image: Marco Zanoli (Sidonius) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karte_Hoch_und_Niederburgund_EN.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>879 CE – 933 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vienne</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Boso of Provence, Louis the Blind, Hugh of Arles</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Provence (Boso), Cisjurane Burgundy</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=906&amp;focus=kingdom-of-lower-burgundy" aria-label="Kingdom of Lower Burgundy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4824 619 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Lower Burgundy lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5144 875L5054 728M5144 875L5111 886"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M5111 886h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5144 875h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5144 875h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=906&amp;focus=kingdom-of-lower-burgundy">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
